{
  "$schema": "../../../node_modules/tourwright/schema/script.schema.json",
  "title": "Meet Tourwright",
  "subtitle": "Narrated videos of your real app, reviewed in Muse",
  "lexicon": {
    "Tourwright": "Tour-right",
    "Next.js": "Next J S",
    "Vite": "Veet",
    "MP4": "M P 4"
  },
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "what",
      "stage": "dashboard",
      "say": "[open]Tourwright makes narrated videos of your app, using your real React components. [how]You write a script. Tourwright speaks it with a voice that runs on your machine, moves a camera around your own interface, and renders an MP4. [this]This video was made with it.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "open",
          "camera": {
            "to": "all"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "how",
          "camera": {
            "to": "stats",
            "zoom": "fit"
          },
          "highlight": "stats",
          "animate": "counts"
        },
        {
          "at": "this",
          "camera": {
            "to": "all"
          },
          "highlight": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "install",
      "stage": "terminal",
      "say": "[install]To start, add Tourwright to a Next.js or Vite React app. [init]Then run init. [files]It creates a config, a starter stage, an intro script, and a skill for your coding agent.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "install",
          "camera": {
            "to": "all"
          },
          "highlight": "install"
        },
        {
          "at": "init",
          "highlight": "init"
        },
        {
          "at": "files",
          "highlight": "init-files"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "stage",
      "stage": "stages-file",
      "say": "[stage]A stage is your real component, rendered with sample data, so there's no login and no server to run. [values]Stages can have values that move, like a meter filling up or a toggle switching on.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "stage",
          "camera": {
            "to": "all"
          },
          "highlight": "imports"
        },
        {
          "at": "values",
          "highlight": "values"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "script",
      "stage": "script-file",
      "say": "[scenes]The script is a list of scenes. Each one names a stage and says what to narrate. [cues]A marker in the narration is a cue. [beats]At each cue, the camera moves, the narration box outlines what you're talking about, or a value animates.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "scenes",
          "camera": {
            "to": "all"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "cues",
          "highlight": "say",
          "camera": {
            "to": "say",
            "zoom": "fit"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "beats",
          "highlight": "beat",
          "camera": {
            "to": "beat",
            "zoom": "fit"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent",
      "stage": "agent",
      "say": "[agent]You rarely write any of this by hand. [steps]Ask your coding agent for a video, and the skill tells it how to plan the scenes, build the stage, and check its work.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "agent",
          "camera": {
            "to": "all"
          },
          "highlight": "prompt"
        },
        {
          "at": "steps",
          "highlight": "agent-steps"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "make",
      "stage": "make-review",
      "say": "[make]One command, make, does the rest. [check]It checks the script and takes a still of every moment, to catch blank or hidden screens. [render]Then it renders the video. [muse]And it opens Muse in your browser.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "make",
          "camera": {
            "to": "all"
          },
          "highlight": "make"
        },
        {
          "at": "check",
          "highlight": "make-check"
        },
        {
          "at": "render",
          "highlight": "make-render"
        },
        {
          "at": "muse",
          "highlight": "make-muse"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "muse",
      "stage": "muse",
      "say": "[muse]Muse is where you review the video. [player]It plays with the narration and captions. [strip]Go scene by scene, at any speed, or loop one scene.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "muse",
          "camera": {
            "to": "muse-window",
            "zoom": "fit"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "player",
          "highlight": "player",
          "animate": "playhead"
        },
        {
          "at": "strip",
          "camera": {
            "to": "transport",
            "zoom": "width",
            "align": "top"
          },
          "highlight": "scrubber"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "notes",
      "stage": "muse",
      "say": "[note]See something to change? Press N. [pinned]The note is pinned to that exact moment, to the millisecond. [box]You can also draw a box around any part of the screen, and the note keeps a picture of it.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "note",
          "camera": {
            "to": "muse-window",
            "zoom": "fit"
          },
          "highlight": "composer",
          "animate": "muse"
        },
        {
          "at": "pinned",
          "highlight": "note-a1",
          "animate": "muse"
        },
        {
          "at": "box",
          "highlight": "note-b2",
          "animate": "muse"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "boxes",
      "stage": "muse",
      "say": "[track]You can place narration boxes too. [add]Add one on anything, then drag its edges to time it. [snap]They snap to the start of a sentence.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "track",
          "camera": {
            "to": "transport",
            "zoom": "width",
            "align": "top"
          },
          "highlight": "box-track"
        },
        {
          "at": "add",
          "highlight": "new-box",
          "animate": "muse"
        },
        {
          "at": "snap",
          "animate": "muse",
          "highlight": "new-box"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "send",
      "stage": "muse",
      "say": "[send]When you're ready, send your notes to the agent.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "send",
          "camera": {
            "to": "muse-window",
            "zoom": "fit"
          },
          "highlight": "send-bar"
        },
        {
          "at": "end",
          "animate": "muse",
          "highlight": "review"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-loop",
      "stage": "agent-loop",
      "say": "[wait]It's been waiting for you. [reply]It makes each change and replies on each note.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "wait",
          "camera": {
            "to": "all"
          },
          "highlight": "wait-notes"
        },
        {
          "at": "reply",
          "highlight": "reply"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fixed",
      "stage": "muse",
      "say": "[fixed]You approve each fix, or say it isn't fixed yet.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "fixed",
          "camera": {
            "to": "muse-window",
            "zoom": "fit"
          },
          "highlight": "note-a1",
          "animate": "muse"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "approve",
      "stage": "muse",
      "say": "[approve]When the video is right, approve it. [dialog]Muse asks whether to render the final video, and lists anything still in progress, so nothing unfinished goes out by accident. [progress]It renders with the real voice. [ready]Then the final video is ready to play or share.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "approve",
          "highlight": "approve",
          "animate": "muse"
        },
        {
          "at": "dialog",
          "highlight": "dialog",
          "animate": "muse"
        },
        {
          "at": "progress",
          "highlight": "render-status",
          "animate": [
            "muse",
            "rendered"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": "ready",
          "highlight": "render-status",
          "animate": "muse"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "wrap",
      "stage": "dashboard",
      "say": "[covers]An approval covers everything the video is made from: the script, the stage, and your components. If any of them changes, Muse asks you to look again. [yours]To make your own, install Tourwright and ask your agent for a video.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "at": "covers",
          "camera": {
            "to": "tasks",
            "zoom": "fit"
          },
          "highlight": "tasks"
        },
        {
          "at": "yours",
          "highlight": false,
          "camera": {
            "to": "all"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
